<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benedict of Aniane</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 747–821</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benedict of Aniane was a Visigothic noble turned monk who founded the abbey of Aniane in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and became the chief monastic reformer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>, first in Aquitaine and then as emperor, he imposed the Rule of Saint Benedict on the monasteries of the empire. Louis founded the abbey of Inda, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kornelimunster">Kornelimünster</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> for him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benedict-of-aniane.jpg" alt="Benedict of Aniane" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Havang(nl) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aniane_(H%C3%A9rault,_Fr)_%C3%A9glise,statue_St._Beno%C3%AEt_d%27Aniane.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 814 Emperor Louis the Pious founded a monastery at Inda, near his palace at Aachen, for <b>Benedict of Aniane</b>, the leading reformer of Frankish monasticism.</blockquote><a href="/state/imperial-abbey-of-kornelimunster">Imperial Abbey of Kornelimünster</a></li><li><blockquote>Louis governed with Frankish counts and advisers, reformed monasteries with <b>Benedict of Aniane</b> and led campaigns into Spain, taking Barcelona in 801.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-aquitaine">Kingdom of Aquitaine</a></li></ul></section>
